al regulator of symbiotic nodule development regulated by microRNA169 in <italic>Medicago truncatula</italic></article-title><source>Genes &#x00026; Development</source><year>2006</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>3084</fpage><lpage>3088</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17114582</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1101/gad.402806</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Middleton</surname><given-names>PH</given-names></name><name><surname>Jakab</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Penmetsa</surname><given-names>RV</given-names></name><name><surname>Starker</surname><given-names>CG</given-names></name><name><surname>Doll</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kal&#x000f3;</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Prabhu</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Marsh</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Mitra</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Kereszt</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Dudas</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>VandenBosch</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Long</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><name><surname>Cook</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><name><surname>Kiss</surname><given-names>GB</given-names></name><name><surname>Oldroyd</surname><given-names>GE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An ERF transcription factor in Medicago truncatula that is essential for Nod factor signal transduction</article-title><source>Plant Cell</source><year>2007</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>1221</fpage><lpage>1234</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17449807</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1105/tpc.106.048264</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Riechmann</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Heard</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Reuber</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Jiang</surname><given-names>CZ</given-names></name><name><surname>Keddie</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Adam</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Pineda</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Ratcliffe</surname><given-names>OJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Samaha</surname><given-names>RR</given-names></name><name><surname>Creelman</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Pilgrim</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Broun</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>JZ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ghandehari</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Sherman</surname><given-names>BK</given-names></name><name><surname>Yu</surname><given-names>GL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Arabidopsis transcription factors: Genome-wide comparative analysis among eukaryotes</article-title><source>Science</source><year>2000</year><volume>290</volume><fpage>2105</fpage><lpage>2110</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11118137</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1126/science.290.5499.2105</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Udvardi</surname><given-names>MK</given-names></name><name><surname>Kakar</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Wandrey</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Montanari</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Murray</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Andriankaja</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>J